course: dictionary
lesson: 3736
title: Flop: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Flop is a good example.
explain: «A happy rabbit may do a binky, leaping and twisting in the air, or flop suddenly onto its side to rest.» Here flop means to drop down loosely and suddenly. The clue is rest: the rabbit lets its body fall.
explain: «The buzz is short and the crash is real, then a flop like a wet sock.» Here a flop is a sudden drop in energy, when you go limp and give up. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: Flop is a verb and a noun: you flop down, and a flop is something that fails.
fact: «Flop» means to fall or sit down heavily and loosely, because you are tired.
fact: «Flop» can also mean to hang down loosely, or to fail completely.
fact: A flop is something that fails completely, like a film nobody wants to watch.
fact: A flip-flop is a sandal, and a belly flop is a dive that lands on your tummy.
exercise: «After school, the children flop onto the sofa, tired out.» What does flop mean here? | Count to ten | Shout loudly at the television | Jump up and run outside | *Fall or sit down heavily and loosely, because they are tired
exercise: «The new show was a total flop, and nobody watched it.» What is a flop here? | A dance move | A kind of sandal | *Something that fails completely | A big meal
exercise: What is a belly flop? | A sleepy yawn | A sort of flip-flop | *A dive that lands on your tummy | A slow walk around the park
test: «The dog flops on its back for a belly rub.» What does flops mean here? | Digs a hole in the garden | *Lies down loosely | Runs quickly across the grass | Barks loudly at the postman
test: In «The plan was a flop», what kind of word is flop? | Adjective | Adverb | *Noun | Verb
exam: Which sentence uses flop to mean something failed? | «Her flip-flops are wet from the pool.» | «The rabbit flopped onto its side to rest.» | *«The plan was a flop, and nobody joined in.» | «She flopped onto her bed after a long day.»
